TOP ACCESS LINK QUALITY CHANGES
------------------------------------------------------------
idx | vehicle | previousGateway | currentGateway | prevAvailable | currAvailable | prevDistance | currDistance | prevPhiLink | currPhiLink | prevQ | currQ | deltaQ | transition

------------------------------------------------------------
ACCESS LINK DYNAMICITY INTERPRETATION
------------------------------------------------------------
- Dv(k) now measures only vehicle entry/exit churn.
- Dl(k) is the mean absolute variation of q_v(k) over vehicles present in both consecutive windows.
- q_v(k) = 1 - phi_link(v, activeGateway); unavailable or missing access links have q_v(k) = 0.
- Missing gateways do not create synthetic distance or phi_link metrics; unavailable metrics are rendered as '-'.
- Coverage loss and coverage gain are reported separately from gateway-to-gateway handover.
- Computational candidate additions do not alter Dl(k) when active access links stay unchanged.
- A gateway transition is reported separately. It affects Dl(k) only through the resulting quality variation.

------------------------------------------------------------
HIERARCHICAL BANDWIDTH INTERPRETATION
------------------------------------------------------------
- link constraint: sum bandwidth by candidateId <= candidate.availableBandwidth
- pool constraint: sum bandwidth by poolId <= pool.availableBandwidth
- the pool does not replace the source-aware link limit: both constraints must hold
- EDGE/CLOUD resolve poolId through the active access gateway; V2V uses the explicit DIRECT_V2V binding

